mastery.solution_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.95]
\tikzset{tickmark/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw (0pt,-4pt)--(0pt,4pt);}}}}}
\coordinate (E) at (0,0);
\coordinate (F) at (2.6,0);
\coordinate (D) at (0,2.6);
\draw[tickmark] (E) -- (F);
\draw[tickmark] (D) -- (E);
\draw (F) -- (D);
\coordinate (ea) at ($(E)!0.3cm!(F)$);
\coordinate (eb) at ($(E)!0.3cm!(D)$);
\draw (ea) -- ($(ea)+(eb)-(E)$) -- (eb);
\node[above] at (D) {$D$};
\node[below left] at (E) {$E$};
\node[below right] at (F) {$F$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$DE=EF$, so exactly two sides are equal and $\Delta DEF$ is isosceles.
$\angle DEF=90^{\circ}$, so $\Delta DEF$ is right-angled.
Equal sides sit opposite equal angles: $DE$ is opposite $\angle DFE$ and $EF$ is opposite $\angle EDF$.
$\Delta DEF$ is isosceles and right-angled, with $\angle EDF=\angle DFE$.

