Take a triangle with angles $120^{\circ}$, $30^{\circ}$ and $30^{\circ}$.
Two angles are equal, so the two sides opposite them are equal and the triangle is isosceles.
$120^{\circ}>90^{\circ}$, so the triangle is obtuse-angled, not acute-angled.
